==============================================================================
cross-manifold verdict
==============================================================================
  Both J_atlas(m003) and J_atlas(m006) equal I(X_0) ∩ I(N) for the
  SAME line N = V(x-z, y-2) -- a proper sub-ideal of I(X_0) in both
  cases. The bounded-length atlas does NOT quite recover the exact
  component ideal from either manifold's collisions alone; it
  recovers X_0 together with one universal spurious line, common to
  both manifolds and identical to the spurious line M found in
  m003's earlier (3-identity-only) ambient decomposition.
  N requires y=tr(b)=2, forcing the Fricke matrix B to be parabolic
  (trace 2, repeated eigenvalue 1) -- a plausible but NOT YET PROVED
  source of generic, manifold-independent word-trace coincidences.

